{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ErHDkxFKZpxdUdNj5gQe7E","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd094-nice\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/nice: Run a Program with Modified Scheduling Priority\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  macOS ships nice but the GNU version supports the --adjustment (-n) flag syntax.\n6\t  The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (gnice, installed\n7\t  by coreutils) byte-for-byte on all flag combinations, verified by differential\n8\t  testing via pkg/testutils.\n9\t\n10\tgoals:\n11\t  - G1: Run a command with an adjusted scheduling priority (nice value).\n12\t  - G2: Print the current nice value when invoked without a command.\n13\t  - G3: Verify functional parity against gnice via differential testing.\n14\t\n15\trequirements:\n16\t  R1:\n17\t    title: Priority adjustment\n18\t    items:\n19\t      - R1.1:\n20\t          text: Must run COMMAND with its scheduling priority adjusted by the given increment. Default increment is 10 (lower priority).\n21\t      - R1.2:\n22\t          text: \"-n ADJUST or --adjustment=ADJUST must set the priority increment. ADJUST may be negative (requires privileges) or positive.\"\n23\t      - R1.3:\n24\t          text: When invoked with no COMMAND, must print the current nice value to stdout and exit 0.\n25\t      - R1.4:\n26\t          text: Must pass all remaining arguments after COMMAND as arguments to the executed command.\n27\t\n28\t  R2:\n29\t    title: Exit codes\n30\t    items:\n31\t      - R2.1:\n32\t          text: Must exit with the exit status of COMMAND when COMMAND completes.\n33\t      - R2.2:\n34\t          text: Must exit 125 when the adjustment is invalid or nice(2) fails. Must exit 126 when COMMAND is found but cannot be invoked. Must exit 127 when COMMAND is not found.\n35\t      - R2.3:\n36\t          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n37\t\n38\tnon_goals:\n39\t  - cmd/nice does not implement real-time scheduling priorities.\n40\t\n41\tacceptance_criteria:\n42\t  - id: AC1\n43\t    criterion: \"nice echo hello runs echo with default +10 priority, matching gnice.\"\n44\t    traces:\n45\t      - R1.1\n46\t      - R1.4\n47\t  - id: AC2\n48\t    criterion: \"nice -n 5 echo hello adjusts priority by 5, matching gnice.\"\n49\t    traces:\n50\t      - R1.2\n51\t  - id: AC3\n52\t    criterion: \"Differential test against gnice passes for all required test cases.\"\n53\t    traces:\n54\t      - R1.1\n55\t      - R1.2\n56\t      - R1.3\n57\t  - id: AC4\n58\t    criterion: \"cmd/nice compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n59\t    traces:\n60\t      - R1.1\n61\t      - R1.2\n62\t      - R1.3\n63\t      - R1.4\n64\t      - R2.1\n65\t      - R2.2\n66\t      - R2.3\n67\t\n68\tpackage_contract:\n69\t  imports:\n70\t    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n71\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"47b6a1f9-5b35-4489-8bbd-2cd2781a6546","uuid":"a0badaf6-54e5-4285-b2a2-26873daa22fa","timestamp":"2026-05-24T03:02:45.818Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5565/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd094-nice.yaml","content":"id: srd094-nice\ntitle: \"cmd/nice: Run a Program with Modified Scheduling Priority\"\n\nproblem: |\n  macOS ships nice but the GNU version supports the --adjustment (-n) flag syntax.\n  The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (gnice, installed\n  by coreutils) byte-for-byte on all flag combinations, verified by differential\n  testing via pkg/testutils.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Run a command with an adjusted scheduling priority (nice value).\n  - G2: Print the current nice value when invoked without a command.\n  - G3: Verify functional parity against gnice via differential testing.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Priority adjustment\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: Must run COMMAND with its scheduling priority adjusted by the given increment. Default increment is 10 (lower priority).\n      - R1.2:\n          text: \"-n ADJUST or --adjustment=ADJUST must set the priority increment. ADJUST may be negative (requires privileges) or positive.\"\n      - R1.3:\n          text: When invoked with no COMMAND, must print the current nice value to stdout and exit 0.\n      - R1.4:\n          text: Must pass all remaining arguments after COMMAND as arguments to the executed command.\n\n  R2:\n    title: Exit codes\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: Must exit with the exit status of COMMAND when COMMAND completes.\n      - R2.2:\n          text: Must exit 125 when the adjustment is invalid or nice(2) fails. Must exit 126 when COMMAND is found but cannot be invoked. Must exit 127 when COMMAND is not found.\n      - R2.3:\n          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/nice does not implement real-time scheduling priorities.\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"nice echo hello runs echo with default +10 priority, matching gnice.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.4\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"nice -n 5 echo hello adjusts priority by 5, matching gnice.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.2\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"Differential test against gnice passes for all required test cases.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"cmd/nice compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n\npackage_contract:\n  imports:\n    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n","numLines":71,"startLine":1,"totalLines":71}}}
