{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user submitted a cobbler orchestrator stitch task (Task ID: 5565) to implement error handling and differential tests for `cmd/nice` in the go-unix-utils project. Specifically:\n   - Implement srd094 R2.1: error handling for invalid adjustment values (non-numeric, out of range) with correct stderr messages\n   - Implement srd094 R2.2: error handling for command not found (exit 127) and command not executable (exit 126)\n   - Implement srd094 R2.3: differential tests against `gnice` reference binary using `testutils.RunDiffTests`\n   - Files: modify `cmd/nice/main.go`, create `cmd/nice/nice_test.go`\n   - Acceptance criteria: tests pass, differential tests compare against gnice, graceful skip when gnice missing, exit codes 125/126/127 match GNU nice behavior\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing pattern: compare Go binary output against GNU reference binary (`gnice`)\n   - `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests`, `testutils.BuildBinary`, `testutils.DiffTest` struct\n   - `exec.LookPath` with `t.Skip` for graceful reference binary absence handling\n   - `syscall.Exec` for process replacement (nice executes the command by replacing itself)\n   - `syscall.Getpriority`/`syscall.Setpriority` for nice value manipulation\n   - Exit code conventions: 125 (internal nice error), 126 (command found but not executable), 127 (command not found)\n   - SIGPIPE handling via `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - Binary name normalization in test stderr comparison (`normalizeBinaryName`)\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd094-nice.yaml`\n     - Defines all requirements for cmd/nice including R1 (priority adjustment), R2 (exit codes)\n     - R2.1: exit with COMMAND's exit status; R2.2: exit 125/126/127 for respective errors; R2.3: SIGPIPE handling\n     - Non-goals: no real-time scheduling priorities\n   \n   - `cmd/nice/main.go` (164 lines, already exists)\n     - Already implements core functionality: parseArgs, priority adjustment, command execution via syscall.Exec\n     - Already has error handling: exit 125 for invalid adjustment/nice failure, exit 127 for command not found, exit 126 for exec failure\n     - Has SIGPIPE handler installed\n     - Full code is available in conversation (lines 1-163)\n     - Key functions: `main()` (lines 32-75), `parseArgs()` (lines 77-163)\n   \n   - `cmd/nice/nice_test.go` (199 lines, already exists despite task saying \"create\")\n     - Already has comprehensive differential tests: no_args, default_adjustment, custom adjustments (-n 5, -n 0, --adjustment=3, --adjustment 3, -n7, -5), command_not_found (exit 127), command_preserves_exit_code (false→exit 1), invalid_adjustment (exit 125), double_dash, large_positive_adjustment, command_args_passed\n     - Has `normalizeBinaryName` normalizer for stderr comparison\n     - Has `TestSIGPIPE` test\n     - Uses `exec.LookPath(\"gnice\")` with `t.Skip` pattern\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet - only file reads were performed before the summary was requested.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Initial investigation reveals that both `cmd/nice/main.go` and `cmd/nice/nice_test.go` already exist with substantial implementations covering most of the task requirements. The task description says nice_test.go action is \"create\" but it already exists with 14 test cases. The main.go already handles exit codes 125/126/127. Need to determine what specific changes are still needed - possibly error message formatting to exactly match GNU nice output, or additional edge case handling.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - First message: The full stitch task description with all context (project documentation, SRDs, architecture, requirements, constrai